-- Form: see the header of ccc23-assessment.l4. Seam (rule R2 of PLAN.md section 3): which offences subsection 486.4(1) refers to is another part's answer, taken as the input
-- `s 486.4(1) the offence is referred to in subsection 486.4(1)` (MAYBE BOOLEAN). Section 163.1 is named by number, so it is tested against the core record `Provision of the Code` (rule R1).

§ `Section 672.501 -- Order restricting publication`

-- 672.501(1): where a Review Board holds a hearing referred to in section 672.5 in respect of an accused who has been declared NCR or unfit to stand trial for an offence referred to in subsection 486.4(1), the Review Board shall make an order directing that
-- any information that could identify a victim, or a witness who is under the age of eighteen years, shall not be published in any document or broadcast or transmitted in any way.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13640 | 672.501 (1) Where a Review Board holds a hearing referred to in section 672.5 in respect of an accused who has been declared not crimi­nally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial for an offence referred to in subsection 486.4(1), the Review Board shall make an order directing that any information that could identify a victim, or a witness who is under the age of eighteen years, shall not be published in any document or broadcast or transmitted in any way.
@ref s 672.501(1) (src:13640)
GIVEN `a Review Board holds a hearing referred to in section 672.5 in respect of an accused who has been declared not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is referred to in subsection 486.4(1), by s 486.4(1) the offence is referred to in subsection 486.4(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.501(1) the Review Board must make an order restricting publication of information that could identify a victim or a witness under eighteen` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a Review Board holds a hearing referred to in section 672.5 in respect of an accused who has been declared not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a Review Board holds a hearing referred to in section 672.5 in respect of an accused who has been declared not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial"
        IF `the offence is referred to in subsection 486.4(1), by s 486.4(1) the offence is referred to in subsection 486.4(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the offence is referred to in subsection 486.4(1), by s 486.4(1) the offence is referred to in subsection 486.4(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for an offence referred to in subsection 486.4(1)"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an offence referred to in subsection 486.4(1)"

-- 672.501(2): the same where the offence is one referred to in section 163.1: the order directs that any information that could identify a witness who is under the age of eighteen years, or any person who is the subject of a representation, written material or a recording
-- that constitutes child sexual abuse and exploitation material within the meaning of section 163.1, shall not be published.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13642 | (2) Where a Review Board holds a hearing referred to in section 672.5 in respect of an accused who has been declared not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial for an offence referred to in section 163.1, a Review Board shall make an order directing that any information that could identify a witness who is under the age of eighteen years, or any person who is the subject of a representation, written material or a recording that constitutes child sexual abuse and exploitation material within the meaning of section 163.1, shall not be published in any document or broadcast or transmitted in any way.
@ref s 672.501(2) (src:13642)
GIVEN `a Review Board holds a hearing referred to in section 672.5 in respect of an accused who has been declared not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      offence IS A `Provision of the Code`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.501(2) the Review Board must make an order restricting publication of information that could identify a witness under eighteen or a person who is the subject of child sexual abuse and exploitation material` MEANS
    IF `a Review Board holds a hearing referred to in section 672.5 in respect of an accused who has been declared not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial` AND offence's `section` EQUALS 163.1
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for an offence referred to in section 163.1"

-- 672.501(3): where a Review Board holds a hearing referred to in section 672.5 for an offence other than those referred to in (1) or (2), on application of the prosecutor, a victim or a witness, the Review Board may make an order directing that any information that could identify the victim or witness
-- shall not be published, if the Review Board is satisfied that the order is necessary for the proper administration of justice.
-- fork: F-GRANT-IF
-- src:13644 | (3) Where a Review Board holds a hearing referred to in section 672.5 in respect of an accused who has been declared not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial for an offence other than the offences referred to in subsection (1) or (2), on application of the prosecutor, a victim or a witness, the Review Board may make an order directing that any information that could identify the victim or witness shall not be published in any document or broadcast or transmitted in any way if the Review Board is satisfied that the order is necessary for the proper administration of justice.
@ref s 672.501(3) (src:13644)
GIVEN `a Review Board holds a hearing referred to in section 672.5 in respect of an accused who has been declared not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial for an offence other than the offences referred to in subsection (1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor, a victim or a witness applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Review Board is satisfied that the order is necessary for the proper administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.501(3) the Review Board may make an order restricting publication of information that could identify the victim or witness` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a Review Board holds a hearing referred to in section 672.5 in respect of an accused who has been declared not criminally responsible on account of mental disorder or unfit to stand trial for an offence other than the offences referred to in subsection (1) or (2)` AND `the prosecutor, a victim or a witness applies`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for an offence other than the offences referred to in subsection (1) or (2), on application of the prosecutor, a victim or a witness"
        IF `the Review Board is satisfied that the order is necessary for the proper administration of justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the Review Board is satisfied that the order is necessary for the proper administration of justice"

-- 672.501(4): an order made under any of subsections (1) to (3) does not apply in respect of the disclosure of information in the course of the administration of justice if it is not the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known in the community.
-- src:13646 | (4) An order made under any of subsections (1) to (3) does not apply in respect of the disclosure of information in the course of the administration of justice if it is not the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known in the community.
@ref s 672.501(4) (src:13646)
GIVEN `it is the disclosure of information in the course of the administration of justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known in the community` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.501(4) the order applies in respect of the disclosure of information` MEANS
    IF `it is the disclosure of information in the course of the administration of justice` AND (NOT `it is the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known in the community`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not apply in respect of the disclosure of information in the course of the administration of justice if it is not the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known in the community"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is not the purpose of the disclosure to make the information known in the community"

