GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.501(7) the Review Board may hold a hearing, in private, to determine whether an order should be made` MEANS
    IF `it is to determine whether an order under subsection 672.501(3) should be made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to determine whether an order under subsection (3) should be made"

-- 672.501(8): in determining whether to make an order under subsection (3), the Review Board shall consider (a) the right to a fair and public hearing; (b) whether there is a real and substantial risk that the victim or witness would suffer significant harm if their identity were disclosed;
-- (c) whether the victim or witness needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation; (d) society's interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses; (e) whether effective alternatives are available;
-- (f) the salutary and deleterious effects of the proposed order; (g) the impact of the proposed order on the freedom of expression of those affected by it; and (h) any other factor that the Review Board considers relevant.
-- src:13656 | (8) In determining whether to make an order under subsection (3), the Review Board shall consider
-- src:13657 | (a) the right to a fair and public hearing;
-- src:13658 | (b) whether there is a real and substantial risk that the victim or witness would suffer significant harm if their identity were disclosed;
-- src:13659 | (c) whether the victim or witness needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation;
-- src:13660 | (d) society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process;
-- src:13661 | (e) whether effective alternatives are available to protect the identity of the victim or witness;
-- src:13662 | (f) the salutary and deleterious effects of the proposed order;
-- src:13663 | (g) the impact of the proposed order on the freedom of expression of those affected by it; and
-- src:13664 | (h) any other factor that the Review Board considers relevant.
@ref s 672.501(8); s 672.501(8)(a); s 672.501(8)(b); s 672.501(8)(c); s 672.501(8)(d); s 672.501(8)(e); s 672.501(8)(f); s 672.501(8)(g); s 672.501(8)(h) (src:13656-13664)
GIVEN `the Review Board is determining whether to make an order under subsection 672.501(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the right to a fair and public hearing` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (a)
      `it is whether there is a real and substantial risk that the victim or witness would suffer significant harm if their identity were disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (b)
      `it is whether the victim or witness needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (c)
      `it is society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (d)
      `it is whether effective alternatives are available to protect the identity of the victim or witness` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (e)
      `it is the salutary and deleterious effects of the proposed order` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (f)
      `it is the impact of the proposed order on the freedom of expression of those affected by it` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (g)
      `it is any other factor that the Review Board considers relevant` IS A BOOLEAN   -- (h)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.501(8) the Review Board must consider the factor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the Review Board is determining whether to make an order under subsection 672.501(3)` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "In determining whether to make an order under subsection (3)"
        IF `it is the right to a fair and public hearing` OR `it is whether there is a real and substantial risk that the victim or witness would suffer significant harm if their identity were disclosed` OR `it is whether the victim or witness needs the order for their security or to protect them from intimidation or retaliation` OR `it is society’s interest in encouraging the reporting of offences and the participation of victims and witnesses in the criminal justice process` OR `it is whether effective alternatives are available to protect the identity of the victim or witness` OR `it is the salutary and deleterious effects of the proposed order` OR `it is the impact of the proposed order on the freedom of expression of those affected by it` OR `it is any other factor that the Review Board considers relevant` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a factor that the Review Board does not consider relevant is not named

