    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in relation to proceedings taken against any person who fails to comply with the order"

§ `Section 672.5011 -- Variation or revocation of order`

-- 672.5011(1): the Review Board shall -- on application of the person who is the subject of an order made under section 672.501 or of any other person, including a prosecutor, who is acting on their behalf, and without holding a hearing -- vary or revoke the order,
-- unless the Review Board is of the opinion that to do so may affect the privacy interests of any person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication of information that could identify that person.
-- fork: F-DUTY-GATE
-- src:13677 | 672.5011 (1) The Review Board shall — on application of the person who is the subject of an order made under section 672.501 or of any other person, including a prosecutor, who is acting on their behalf, and without holding a hearing — vary or revoke the order, unless the Review Board is of the opinion that to do so may affect the privacy interests of any person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication in any document or the broadcasting or transmission in any way of information that could identify that person.
@ref s 672.5011(1) (src:13677)
GIVEN `the person who is the subject of an order made under section 672.501, or another person acting on their behalf, applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Review Board is of the opinion that to vary or revoke the order may affect the privacy interests of any person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication of information that could identify that person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 672.5011(1) the Review Board must vary or revoke the order without holding a hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person who is the subject of an order made under section 672.501, or another person acting on their behalf, applies` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on application of the person who is the subject of an order made under section 672.501 or of any other person, including a prosecutor, who is acting on their behalf"
        IF `the Review Board is of the opinion that to vary or revoke the order may affect the privacy interests of any person who is the subject of any order prohibiting the publication of information that could identify that person` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Review Board is of the opinion that to do so may affect the privacy interests of any person"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

